# UI tooltips

When the user asks for a tooltip (or hover tip / help text on hover), use **our** immediate tooltip — not the browser's native `title` tooltip.

## Do

- Prefer `has-icon-tip` on the host + `<IconTip>…</IconTip>` when the control sits inside scrollable panels, detail panes, or other overflow clipping ancestors.
- Use inline `has-icon-tip` + `<span className="icon-tip" role="tooltip">…</span>` only when no clipping ancestors exist.
- Add `icon-tip-below` (or let `IconTip` auto-flip) when upward placement would clip (top bar, header nav, phase nav, sticky headers).
- Use `level-card-tip` only where that richer pattern already applies (Engine level cards).
- Tips should appear immediately on hover / focus-visible (see `.icon-tip` in `src/index.css`), including on disabled hosts.

## Don't

- Do **not** use `title=` / native browser tooltips for hover help (delayed, inconsistent look).
- Do not invent a third tooltip system without an explicit request.

